{"documentary": {"label": "Documentary", "voice": "George", "src": "assets/builder/voice/documentary.mp3", "duration": 59.21, "peaks": [1.0, 0.901, 0.463, 0.682, 0.778, 0.886, 0.681, 0.785, 0.866, 0.11, 0.758, 0.927, 0.836, 0.928, 0.895, 0.504, 0.896, 0.814, 0.59, 0.754, 0.902, 0.68, 0.662, 0.743, 0.752, 0.566, 0.039, 0.994, 0.684, 0.651, 0.812, 0.405, 0.82, 0.724, 0.865, 0.68, 0.393, 0.887, 0.843, 0.752, 0.696, 0.883, 0.859, 0.67, 0.867, 0.848, 0.455, 0.761, 0.513, 0.613, 0.807, 0.757, 0.64, 0.922, 0.756, 0.669, 0.377, 0.904, 0.803, 0.46, 0.815, 0.955, 0.846, 0.563], "lines": [{"text": "Most of what we write is never read twice.", "start": 0.0, "end": 2.38}, {"text": "Reports, notes, and long articles settle into folders, waiting for a quiet hour that may never come.", "start": 2.38, "end": 8.91}, {"text": "But people listen almost anywhere: during a commute, on a run, or while making dinner.", "start": 8.91, "end": 14.72}, {"text": "VoiceAI begins with that gap.", "start": 14.72, "end": 17.11}, {"text": "It takes a document and does more than read the words aloud, because a page spoken word for word still sounds like a page.", "start": 17.11, "end": 24.52}, {"text": "First, a language model reshapes the material into something meant for listening: shorter sentences, a clearer thread, and a reason to keep going.", "start": 24.52, "end": 33.65}, {"text": "The result can be delivered by a single narrator, or by two hosts trading ideas in the style of a podcast, an interview, or even a debate.", "start": 33.65, "end": 42.82}, {"text": "The tone can shift, too—from a documentary, to a bedtime story, to a true-crime mystery.", "start": 42.82, "end": 49.13}, {"text": "Only after that does a voice bring the words to life.", "start": 49.13, "end": 52.51}, {"text": "What emerges is not a recording of text, but the same idea, told in the way ideas are meant to be heard.", "start": 52.51, "end": 59.21}], "env": [0.17, 0.56, 0.86, 0.74, 0.3, 0.04, 0.14, 0.54, 0.2, 0.55, 0.43, 